From 93fb5c35c46cb331ffb860df38ea2fde47443135 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:18:45 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: add xRX500 GPHY firmware loader

Add the loader that boots the four internal Gigabit PHYs (GPHY 2-5)
of the xRX500 family. The GPHYs are microcontroller cores that
execute firmware staged in DDR; the loader:

 - requests the PHY11G firmware image (the LAN blob - the EVA
   bootloader preloads the WAN blob, which does not serve the LAN
   ports), copies it to a 16 KiB-aligned DMA-visible staging buffer,
   and programs its physical address into the per-GPHY base-address
   registers. The staging address must be a plain physical DDR
   address (dma_alloc_coherent addresses on this platform are not
   GPHY-reachable), and the buffer's device is marked non-coherent
   so the image is actually flushed to DDR before the GPHYs boot.

 - sequences the GPHY resets through the RCU reset controller:
   clear the GPHY-group master reset, then release the per-GPHY
   resets after the base addresses are programmed. When the EVA
   bootloader has already preset base addresses, the loader detects
   and re-stages them coherently instead of double-resetting.

 - exposes xrx500_gphy_fw_is_loaded() so the MDIO bus driver can
   defer PHY enumeration until the GPHYs are running.

Ported from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198),
drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/xrx500_phy_fw.c - Copyright (C) 2012
John Crispin <blogic@openwrt.org> (notice restored), updated to
v6.18 reset-controller and firmware APIs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
